{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm","id":1387325,"title":"Are Generations really worthwhile in VTM?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-10T14:08:55-07:00","id":1387325,"title":"Are Generations really worthwhile in VTM?","content":"I know Generations has both a mechanic and metaplot staple of the game.. but I feel as if its a mistake entirely. From the meta, PCs and many NPCs alike are just going to be weaker and weaker until &quot;Gehenna&quot; happens because too much Kindred have become high generation. Generation to me feels to profoundly limiting to me, though atleast with a caveat you can lower it from diablerie- but thats pratical suicide since anyone can see your aura with Auspex and tell you've committed Amaranth easily. You could go be Autarkis after, but then that'll just anger alot of people at once and have a blood hunt on you. Thinbloods realistically can never be viable in full Vampiric society since their basically only a small minuscule step up from ghouls by all means. The whole &quot;Thinblood&quot; alchemy (a discipline only ever added to make somewhat appealing) can't pull weight for the other things they severely lack.<br /> <br /> This is why I feel VTR did a good job of this- realistically as you grow older and survive through the centuries, you get stronger in VTR and your childe (even though that maybe a detriment later on for your character) have a chance of getting stronger too, not gimped on embrace. IDK feel free to bash me if you think this post is stupid (with considering how integral Generation is to VTM)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 05-10-2020, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T14:19:10-07:00","id":1387327,"title":"","content":"Part of the attraction of VtM vs VtR was the fact that Generation meant that elders where flat out more powerful, that feeling that the elders and up had everything in their favour due to age, power and experience, and yet you want to kill and eat them anyway, you have to chase that same power...yeah that feeling is cool, that kind of knowing it's pointless but doing it anyway, to rage against the fall of night.<br /> <br /> VtR went with Potency, which was and is a different mood entirely, and cool, of you like it, VtR is still ongoing, still a live system, but the two systems don't play well together. VtM Methuselahs are basically Elder Gods, with the Antes as the Outer Gods and Caine as basically Azathoth, that horror of being lunch for something unstoppable, that doesn't register you in anyway, was awesome, it's Cosmic Horror, which I love ( and Obtenerbration used to really riff on that, as did Viscittitude).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T14:28:39-07:00","id":1387330,"title":"","content":"The stains on your aura temporary. Either one year or the difference in generations between the two of you. Depending on how time flows in one's game it may or may not be an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:06:22-07:00","id":1387337,"title":"","content":"1 year alone is a LONG time for neonates and even to an extent a semi-seasoned Anchillae, much more particularly for higher gen Kindred. From an OOC and also IC standpoint, there is legitimately no incentive for diablerie for how long it lasts. One Kindred gifted in Auspex sees you and a whole rumor mill goes about the PC in question throughout the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:07:15-07:00","id":1387340,"title":"","content":"Yes. Which is why the Elders must surrender their blood to my tummy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:27:26-07:00","id":1387347,"title":"","content":"So long as you can get a couple of sanctioned ones, a spot of recreational diablerie can be good for fun and profit...<br /> <br /> Don't go for the elders though, just work your way up slowly, let them use you till you're ready for them...<br /> <br /> I think the whole wishy washy up and down potency was just a terrible idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:28:20-07:00","id":1387348,"title":"","content":"\u201cAge beats generation. Cunning beats age. Respect beats everything.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:32:44-07:00","id":1387350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Riccardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387348#post1387348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cAge beats generation. Cunning beats age. Respect beats everything.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Except guns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:44:30-07:00","id":1387351,"title":"","content":"Generations helps creating an important thematic point : you will never be stronger than your maker. <br /> <br /> This is really important, since without the huge gap between generations some of the main themes of the game (the manipulation of the ancients, the Jyhad, and revenges running throug lineages) would not be developed in the same way (there is a reason if there is no Jyhad in Requiem, but just Covenant warfare)<br /> <br /> As Montano said<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">We do not make ourselves vampires, and we are never as strong as our <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sires\" target=\"_blank\">sires</a>. <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gratiano_de_Veronese\" target=\"_blank\">Gratiano</a> boasts of his strength, but if he could do what the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lasombra_Antediluvian\" target=\"_blank\">founder</a> did, he would, and he does not. There is always a sire to direct us, and a sire beyond him, and so back to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Caine\" target=\"_blank\">Caine</a>. There is no 'destiny' for you to choose but what your masters allow for you.</td> </tr> </table></div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from that,Requiem gives you a rappresentation of libertarian capitalism, where if you play your cards right and wait enough time you will be in power one day. <br /> The Masquerade gives you a rappresentation of crony capitalism or feudalism. No matter how good you are and how much you wait, what it is important is who your father was and who were allies and friends.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:48:14-07:00","id":1387353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387337#post1387337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 year alone is a LONG time for neonates and even to an extent a semi-seasoned Anchillae, much more particularly for higher gen Kindred. From an OOC and also IC standpoint, there is legitimately no incentive for diablerie for how long it lasts. One Kindred gifted in Auspex sees you and a whole rumor mill goes about the PC in question throughout the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>there are enough legal ways to get diablerie (sect wars, bloodhunts)<br /> <br /> if it doesn't work for you, join an anarch diablerist gang, or take a plane for mexico<br /> <br /> another reason the anarchs/sabbat don't run out of new blood<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T17:10:22-07:00","id":1387365,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">I only see one actual question in your post. I'll refuse to take the edition-war bait, and answer that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> </span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm#post1387325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Are Generations really worthwhile in VTM?<br /> <br /> </span></b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">In V20? Yes. Yes, it is.<br /> <br /> If the ST allows you to pick/buy your Generation, get the lowest number you can possibly finagle. The entire species of Cainites is organized around the principle that all power flows from Caine. The closer you are, the better. The stronger the blood, the better your existence is.<br /> <br /> In V5? Well, yes, if you are offered strong blood at chagen, take it. I say this somewhat less enthusiastically. There has been some nerfing afoot in V5.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in other news, hit points are a good thing in D&amp;D, royal flushes are a good thing in poker, and many goals are better than no goals in futbol. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T18:30:04-07:00","id":1387384,"title":"","content":"And thats the whole reason why Generations are bad, it all flows from a character from the Book of Genesis, who was only ever made the &quot;progenitor&quot; of Vampires just for the sake of it because he was the &quot;first murderer&quot; and that sounded cool. Double the fact that in the book of Genesis &quot;Cain&quot; supposedly founded &quot;Enoch&quot; (a fictional city in the Book of Genesis AND Vampire: The Masquerade), which I assume the writers wanted that tie-in because Kindred sustain in and dwell in cities since it has the highest kine concentrations imaginable. (never mind the fact that their were real older cities that predated the development of any of the books regarding &quot;Genesis&quot; and the other series of tales, so how could Cain have Enoch built before these cities without that being touched upon?) VTM should've never went this centralized Abrahamic route, now we're stuck with Generations, with by the meta, will slowly crunch the story down until it can't be ignored and the current VTM writers will have to eventually force Gehenna as per the metaplot no matter what.<br /> <br /> Why of all these things with Caine anyway in the first place? Its so bizarre because Vampires really had little to do with Christianity in folklore by any capacity. At best in some iterations Crosses repelled them, Holy Water burned them, and they couldn't enter holy places. In VTM though Vampires can enter Churches, Crosses don't repel them at all, and they aren't fazed by Holy Water IIRC. The only time Kindred in VTM are hassled by religion is with True Faith- but True Faith can be from any religious interpretation- its clear not only Christian elements can harm Kindred. If thats the case, why have the &quot;curse&quot; by one eeked by the Abrahamic based God be the focal point in the first place when other faiths can affect Kindred? What gives?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 05-10-2020, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T21:22:20-07:00","id":1387407,"title":"","content":"While I don't like the precise implementation, I think V5 did the right thing and made Generation more variable by layering Blood Potency on it. The setting impact of Generation is still there, but especially for higher Generations, age comes into play more effectively than pre-V5 Generation allows. V5 was very smart to have starting Generation be a group decision instead of something bought with creation resources.<br /> <br /> I like VtR's approach even better, but it's not VtM and if I'm playing VtM Generation needs to be a tier mechanic that can't simply be overcome with time.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Noddist mythology on Generations is just that: mythology. It's the dominate mythology in VtM because VtM vampires are predominately from Abrahamic faith influenced cultures. Eastern Asian cultures have different vampires. African vampires actually do have a completely different mythology that there is no way to prove is more or less true than Noddist mythology even if it has far less adherents (and the African vampire culture is to not care as much about the &quot;facts&quot; as much as the lessons the stories teach to bother getting into debates with the Noddists about it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T22:15:02-07:00","id":1387416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387327#post1387327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the attraction of VtM vs VtR was the fact that Generation meant that elders where flat out more powerful, that feeling that the elders and up had everything in their favour due to age, power and experience, and yet you want to kill and eat them anyway, you have to chase that same power...yeah that feeling is cool, that kind of knowing it's pointless but doing it anyway, to rage against the fall of night.<br /> <br /> VtR went with Potency, which was and is a different mood entirely, and cool, of you like it, VtR is still ongoing, still a live system, but the two systems don't play well together. VtM Methuselahs are basically Elder Gods, with the Antes as the Outer Gods and Caine as basically Azathoth, that horror of being lunch for something unstoppable, that doesn't register you in anyway, was awesome, it's Cosmic Horror, which I love ( and Obtenerbration used to really riff on that, as did Viscittitude).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. The two systems reflect the storytelling priorities of the two different games. The frustration of having a parent whose influence you can seemingly never outgrow is not only important to the mood of VtM, it's important to the lore. When elder vampire threw their childer to the first Inquisition in the hopes of covering themselves, it wasn't the fact that they had more money that allowed them to do it. It was an inequality in raw supernatural potential. Without that, there's no Anarch Revolt, which means no Camarilla and no Sabbat.<br /> <br /> It fits with the cynicism of the 1990's that becoming a vampire can turn out to be a drag. Yay, I'm immortal. Oh, but this old monster just wants me to be its henchman forever. Bummer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-11-2020, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T00:13:39-07:00","id":1387427,"title":"","content":"ignoring v5 which flattened everything, the WoD has alway been about exploring seemingly insurmountable hierarchies, inequality, opression, the idea that people are &quot;born&quot; better and so on and so forth. The world of darkness has always been a satire of things wrong with the real world (until recent writings that is) where everything's worse. Ever thought super elites were parasites making money from the labour of others without contributing much themselves? Well now some of them are literally parasites that suck the blood of the people below them. Generation is like the metaphorical way of saying &quot;you're just a millionaire, you can't do shit to a billionaire!&quot; <br /> <br /> If vampires didn't have generation, they'd just live alone, accumulate disciplines, and not bother their equally powerful neighbours all that much. Because you've got a big generational disparity, the older and more powerful vampires can order the younger ones around in a way that has a lot more real world parallels. If you were all equal, anyone could become prince, democracy wouldn't even seem like a bad idea, but being stuck in a facist monarcharchy/theocracy where the rulers take hundreds of years to age out? That's worth exploring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T00:57:00-07:00","id":1387434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387427#post1387427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If vampires didn't have generation, they'd just live alone, accumulate disciplines, and not bother their equally powerful neighbours all that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>As VtR demonstrates... this is hardly true. Older vampires just having way more XP to spend on powers creates the disparities that allows the powerful to force the weak into a social system.<br /> <br /> VtR has different goals, but even without Generation there's hardly equality.<br /> <br /> You're right about certain things. VtM's Generation keeps down much experimenting with different social organization systems, while VtR's Potency system helps the variety its intended to have make sense. Generation is certainly important to the feeling of the setting, but there's lots of ways it could be adjusted without losing what makes it essential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T04:38:35-07:00","id":1387445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387407#post1387407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Noddist mythology on Generations is just that: mythology. It's the dominate mythology in VtM because VtM vampires are predominately from Abrahamic faith influenced cultures. Eastern Asian cultures have different vampires. African vampires actually do have a completely different mythology that there is no way to prove is more or less true than Noddist mythology even if it has far less adherents (and the African vampire culture is to not care as much about the &quot;facts&quot; as much as the lessons the stories teach to bother getting into debates with the Noddists about it).</div> </div> </div> </div>But is it really a mythology though? There have been multiple instances in VTM where they have confirmed Caine to be real in VTM and the grander oWoD universe. (At the top of my head the book where it deliberately centered around the story of Cain, D:TF's shoehorned plot, multiple little tidbits just flat out confirming Caine, parts of Mage via the Celestial Chorus confirming Cain by saying of their own was Lilith, Set being 3rd generation instead of being a 1st gen of its own kind- which basically pulls the rug under Setite creation lore etc). Also the Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom had the curse brought downstream from the Middle-East, which by coupled logic of Abrahamic creationist lore means that &quot;Adam and Eve were the first humans&quot;, which confirms the reality of Cain. This last sentence maybe confusing to stomach the way I phrased it, so heres what I mean (I've touched on this on another old thread of mine): Caine couldn't have been the first murderer since the first humans had tribal wars and small intraconflicts that would result in murder way before the book of Genesis. The first murderer could've been a very archaic human, an african tribesman, a cro-magnon tribesman, or some neanderthal.<br /> <br /> But with VTM making it as such in the oWoD universe with Cain being the actual first murderer, we can glean in-universe from his 3rd generation grandchilder traveling to Africa out of the Middle-East to Africa and then the Americas to spread the curse. If Cain was just myth vampirism would start in a another locale where the first murder DID take place (or not have anything to do with the first &quot;murder&quot; a human has committed since that fiat of mythology came from the Book of Genesis altogether- but since it is a considerable part of VTM that a &quot;first murder&quot; has to take place for Vampirism to start, that by itself confirms Cain as the progenitor of Vampires through sheer Occam Razor because no one else fits the bill or precedent).<br /> <br /> This why I loathe the whole Cain spiel. It hinges on one character that no matter what at some point is going to wreck the entire setting to cull the increasing high generation Kindred (a mechanic and plot device that slugs the setting) and not only cull the Vampires, but probably destroy the entire earth fighting his awakened Antediluvian childer as well. Its one character that nobody would really care about if he didn't have the cool accolade of &quot;first murderer&quot;, which means he'd never be central to VTM. Its a character thats basically the main character, but shrouded entirely and is going only ever to really reveal himself fully when the VTM writers have decided that game has reached its waning era and its time to pull the plug (a thing I remind you they've done before). Its a drag!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 05-11-2020, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T05:00:07-07:00","id":1387448,"title":"","content":"Caine can be the first vampire without literally being the first murderer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T05:00:43-07:00","id":1387449,"title":"","content":"The World of Darkness is steeped in<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermeticism\" target=\"_blank\"> hermetic theory</a>, which means that although parts of the Caine myth are true, it doesn't exclude the Cagn myth that the Liabon believe in. Althought there's a singular &quot;God&quot; it's more &quot;The one above all&quot; rather than something that excludes the Triat and discounts the whole WTA mythology. The Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Demon, Wraith, Eastern mythologies can all simultaneously be true (but you've got to piece it together a bit) <br /> <br /> Similarly, I do like Generation from a religious standpoint. The &quot;we can source outselves back to a blood god&quot; is great. It gives us this feeling that ancient times must've been fantastical, we can look to an imagined past (something that fascists are so fond of). Generation creates a great deal of mystery, whilst not having generation or replacing it with blood potency just gives the impression that there's always been vampires and, although age might've brought them power, it doesn't really have the whole 'unknowable, unreachable blood-god' that generation brings. With generation in place, most vampires look to a 7th gen and realise &quot;I will never be able to get as powerful as them, as their transcendant generation allows them to have more dots and powers beyond five, unless I eat my way up to remove my limits' whilst without generation, you've got something more like &quot;In 300 years I'll be her pier, as percentage wise our ages won't be so different'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T05:12:56-07:00","id":1387450,"title":"","content":"Tbh that whole thing about \u201cAll realities are true simultaneously\u201d gives me a literal headache. I just pick and choose the parts I like (Eden did exist, the great majority of humans in the Antediluvian world are not descended from the people of Eden).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T05:14:00-07:00","id":1387451,"title":"","content":"* \u201cEden did exist, but...\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T05:17:35-07:00","id":1387452,"title":"","content":"The way you put it does sound good, but Generation wouldn't be bad if didn't gimp each succession so badly until we get to the whole Thin-Blood thing. I wished they never came up with Thin-Bloods and just left it at higher generation makes you not stronger than the ones with a lower generation than yourself. It would be extremely hard to pull off from what I understand though, since how high can you take Generation without the Thin-Blood thematic until it mechanically doesn't make sense? Thin-Bloods make sense within the meta and mechanics because:<br /> <br /> A) a generation system like we see in VTM would always have a downstream weakened state as you've mentioned, which will breed interesting conflict<br /> <br /> B) you can't have continuously high gen Vampires without it reflecting someway ICly altogether<br /> <br /> C) its a way for the story to not get bloated because sooner or later Gehenna is going to reset the entire vampire kind<br /> <br /> I feel like this is bad though because the whole dialectic battle between &quot;young and old&quot; is thrown out the window once you get to Thin-Bloods/13+ Gen vampires. These type of vampires can never broach the whole continuous interesting conflict between young vs old because their just too flat-out supernaturally weak to be of any viability. Thats when the setting gets to be a drag when your stuck with these type of vampires that can't be interesting anymore.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also the whole &quot;multi-layer reality&quot; thing was just a cop-out because the writers of D:TF didn't want to explain the full oWoD creation of all the splats, just hamfist their old &quot;Lucifer vs God&quot; conflict into the oWoD universe. No matter how you spin it that splat breaks/retroactively retcons alot of lore from other splats. It was supposed to tie-in the entire setting as whole, but did the exact opposite entirely. I wonder how White Wolf even let D:TF be greenlight considering oWoD was coming to a close at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 05-11-2020, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T05:23:46-07:00","id":1387453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387451#post1387451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* \u201cEden did exist, but...\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the last three posts, its a headache. Caine doesn't necessarily have to be the inventor of murder, I mean Werewolf acknowledges Murder was a thing since caveman times, as the Ananasi genocided the Neanderthals, and Werewolves have been killing their cousins since before humanity crossed the Bearing Straight. And Werewolf have hints of an Edenic holy spot in Ethiopia, but they don't necessarily acknowledge the story of the Garden of Eden. The Chronicles of the Dark Mother talks of Eden just being one Garden of many, and that may be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:28:48-07:00","id":1387513,"title":"","content":"A neonate with 5 dots in generation has a huge target on their head. If a player does put everything into generation, you as a storyteller should make them pay for it with other vampires after their blood. Maybe a Sabbat pack gets wind that an elder has produced a new childer, some jealous anarchs decide to take a wack at them or someone just works to manipulate events into tricking them into a massive masquerade breach so they can get a sanctioned diablerie.<br /> <br /> If you want to go with the whole mage paradigms angle, perhaps Yahwe was originally just another local deity (There's stuff in the actual old testament that supports this). Following this logic, Caine and the deluge were fairly regional things. This could be some early city that formed before the ice ages ended and the &quot;first&quot; city was either buried under the waves when the ice caps began to melt or maybe a massive lake sitting in a glacier broke free and flooded the region. There's some evidence for other events that could have caused flooding around the Mediterranean with volcanic eruptions and a mountain in Italy even fell into the sea. Those could have caused massive tidal surges flooding the coastal areas. So maybe the flood myth is some long remembered local disaster. The whole Caine thing could just be a curse laid by a local God. A God that became very powerful over time as people all over the world began to worship them in some form. The mass worship of Yahwe in it's various forms kept the Vampiric curse around as most of the other fantastic beasts began to become rarer and die out. The whole Adam character could just be a really popular tribal leader where they omitted the rest of the tribe from the story. Hell, there's two accounts of Genesis in the bible that contradict each other. If you want, maybe Set and his get are from a completely separate line and just share a similar curse. Maybe there's something to Ennoia originally being a goddess of beasts and Churka being a night god, or maybe some of the Laibon really do have their own origins and the curses are alike but come from different sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T11:58:04-07:00","id":1387560,"title":"","content":"I feel I need to clarify a bit. <br /> It's not &quot;All realities are true&quot; but rather, each splat has only a small image of the greater truth (But you can't trust vampire, werewolf or mage acounts; that's a game of chinese whispers played by liars and braggarts) and I don't it would do the setting any favours if it's history didn't conflict and could be worked out by players easily. That said, all of the splats share a common theme of &quot;In ancient times our people were basically gods and the environment benefited us massively and now we've lost are way; all the good stuff has waned and everything sucks now. The blood getting weaker each generation is a big part of that. <br /> <br /> Besides, I think vampires were kinda... supposed to eat eachother. That's part of the curse. That's why they fear and loath everything; Because children are bound to eat their parents, and the elders have done their absolute best to put off this natural cycle. If there was no generation, you really wouldn't have that drive. An elder must oppress their children to stop them eating him, the children must eat their elder to escape oppression. It's a wonderful cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T12:05:03-07:00","id":1387562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387427#post1387427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If vampires didn't have generation, they'd just live alone, accumulate disciplines, and not bother their equally powerful neighbours all that much. Because you've got a big generational disparity, the older and more powerful vampires can order the younger ones around in a way that has a lot more real world parallels. If you were all equal, anyone could become prince, democracy wouldn't even seem like a bad idea, but being stuck in a facist monarcharchy/theocracy where the rulers take hundreds of years to age out? That's worth exploring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea isn't to flatten it out completely, but to make it depend on age instead of birth. With this proposed change (Blood Potency instead of Generation), Ur-Shulgi isn't insanely powerful because he was embraced by a third-gen, he's insanely powerful because he was embraced more than five thousand years ago, and has spent large parts of the intervening time becoming arguably the strongest blood-sorcerer in the world.<br /> <br /> In VtM, one of the important themes has always been powerlessness in the face of nigh-omnipotent elders. Even if you survive for five thousand years, you'll never be as strong as Ur-Shulgi is now. You don't have the potential for it. You'll always be limited by the circumstances of your creation, unless you're willing to consume souls for it. Which is great if that's what you're into! It's not a theme I've ever particularly liked, though. It seems to me like someone with five thousand years' worth of xp on their sheet should be insanely powerful just from that alone; they don't need an extra &quot;oh btw I'm also just intrinsically better than you&quot; on top of that.<br /> <br /> And if neonates <i>do</i> have the potential to become the next Helena or Menele\u2014if they survive for millennia without getting killed\u2014it explains nicely why so many of them are willing to buy into the Camarilla's propaganda. Sure, being at the bottom of the hierarchy sucks now, but look, you could be the one in a million that makes it to the top! In terms of real-world parallels, look at the classic American myth of the poor as temporarily disadvantaged millionaires. I don't see how that myth could exist if there's <u>also</u> an immutable, inviolable law in place saying someone of low birth can <i>never</i> rise above their station; the potential needs to be there, in theory, even though 99.999% of neonates will never achieve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T12:08:43-07:00","id":1387563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387445#post1387445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This why I loathe the whole Cain spiel. It hinges on one character that no matter what at some point is going to wreck the entire setting to cull the increasing high generation Kindred (a mechanic and plot device that slugs the setting) and not only cull the Vampires, but probably destroy the entire earth fighting his awakened Antediluvian childer as well. Its one character that nobody would really care about if he didn't have the cool accolade of &quot;first murderer&quot;, which means he'd never be central to VTM. Its a character thats basically the main character, but shrouded entirely and is going only ever to really reveal himself fully when the VTM writers have decided that game has reached its waning era and its time to pull the plug (a thing I remind you they've done before). Its a drag!</div> </div> </div> </div>I also loathe the Caine mythology being treated as fact, but I should add\u2014it's one of the things V5 has tried hardest to retcon. (And some of the pre-V5 stuff too.) Now it's been stated outright that there's no confirmation of the Noddist theory over the Setite one or the Haqimite one, and most Kindred have never read the Book of Nod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T12:41:18-07:00","id":1387570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387427#post1387427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>ignoring v5 which flattened everything, </b>the WoD has alway been about exploring seemingly insurmountable hierarchies, inequality, opression, the idea that people are &quot;born&quot; better and so on and so forth. The world of darkness has always been a satire of things wrong with the real world (until recent writings that is) where everything's worse. Ever thought super elites were parasites making money from the labour of others without contributing much themselves? Well now some of them are literally parasites that suck the blood of the people below them. Generation is like the metaphorical way of saying &quot;you're just a millionaire, you can't do shit to a billionaire!&quot;<br /> <br /> If vampires didn't have generation, they'd just live alone, accumulate disciplines, and not bother their equally powerful neighbours all that much. Because you've got a big generational disparity, the older and more powerful vampires can order the younger ones around in a way that has a lot more real world parallels. If you were all equal, anyone could become prince, democracy wouldn't even seem like a bad idea, but being stuck in a facist monarcharchy/theocracy where the rulers take hundreds of years to age out? That's worth exploring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the note as a mod to say that this is a perfectly valid response and not something that counts as a dig at V5. However, MWIS, have you tried NOT mentioning your disappointment in V5 in any post?<br /> <br /> Because I'd be curious if you could for say...ten posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T12:43:16-07:00","id":1387571,"title":"","content":"Its part of his Jyhad. It is a stalwart endeavor and task.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T16:15:54-07:00","id":1387614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387453#post1387453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with the last three posts, its a headache. Caine doesn't necessarily have to be the inventor of murder, I mean Werewolf acknowledges Murder was a thing since caveman times, as the Ananasi genocided the Neanderthals, and Werewolves have been killing their cousins since before humanity crossed the Bearing Straight. And Werewolf have hints of an Edenic holy spot in Ethiopia, but they don't necessarily acknowledge the story of the Garden of Eden. The Chronicles of the Dark Mother talks of Eden just being one Garden of many, and that may be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the point is Werewolf cosmology does NOT work well with the other splats' cosmology, not Vampire but also not Mage, Wraith or Demon. Note that Mage mentions the stone used by Caine to kill Abel as an extremely powerful magical item and Demon confirms Caine's story and its significance.<br /> <br /> The way I found to make all oWoD splats' cosmologies work together is stealing a page from Mage:the Awakening. If we assume the war between angels and demons was a war where winning battles meant reshaping reality and time we can assume Enoch and the like existed in a &quot;time before time&quot; and the deluge was what happened when the angels won and &quot;fixed&quot; reality and time as they are now (some aspects of the previous realities still exist, the underworld for one). In my games the fera and spirits where pulled &quot;out of time&quot; before the same happened for vampires and the egyptian &quot;gods&quot; (basically mages with no paradox) and God turned himself into the Triat.<br /> It's complicated but it actually makes the cosmology work smoothly.<br /> <br /> IT: Generation was always a problem stat. It defines a character's potential power so at chargen, players who want powerful characters usually want to max it. The other problem is you can't lower generation unless you devour someone's soul and blood, which is a truly evil act. That's great for telling stories about power and how it corrupts but it also means unscrupulous players try their best to diablerize their way to &quot;power&quot;, character development be damned.<br /> <br /> On the other hand generation is an integral part of VtM: blood is power and the older the blood the more powerful its is, which makes it tempting for those who want power above all else and are willing to sacrifice their humanity to get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T17:08:40-07:00","id":1387617,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t mind Caine all that much.<br /> <br /> One of the aspects in Judeo-Christian cosmology is a human soul with free will (i.e. the image and likeness of God) that animals lack (animals have no choice but to follow their nature).<br /> <br /> Similarly, the Catholic Church holds that one of the means by which God could have chosen to create humankind was by setting up the process of evolution and then, at the proper time, breathing a divine soul into one of our ancestors. We know from genetic research that a mitochondrial Eve from which we all descended existed c. 150-200k years ago.<br /> <br /> So who\u2019s to say that \u201cEve\u201d and her mate (called Adam for convenience) couldn\u2019t be the point when God stepped in and finished His creation of humankind by adding free-willed souls to them (if you want to incorporate the Mage cosmology it could be that Adam, Lilith and then Eve were the first to Awaken).<br /> <br /> One of the key elements of murder (vs. a justifiable killing; the proper translation of the Commandment is \u201cThou shalt not murder.\u201d) is free will and intent. Before the addition of a soul, our ancestors lacked the free will to go against their natures; they may have killed others, but lacking intent it couldn\u2019t be considered murder any more than one wolf killing another to secure food or a mate would be considered murder.<br /> <br /> One of Adam and Eve\u2019s descendants though (call him Caine for convenience) used their free will to deliberately end the life of one of their kin (I use \u201cdescendant\u201d and \u201ckin\u201d in place of son and brother because very primitive tribes rarely distinguished generations of ancestors from each other, nor siblings from cousins). This would be the first actual murder.<br /> <br /> Per the Book of Nod, Caine fled to a land where he found Lilith and, one botched attempt at Awakening later, we\u2019ve got the first vampire. The key point here though is that after leaving Lilith he didn\u2019t actually return to realms of men, he first spent an \u201ceon\u201d alone.<br /> <br /> Given the prose it\u2019s unlikely it refers to the recent astronomical usage and is instead, as originally intended, an indeterminately long time; likely well over 100k years, probably slipping in and out of torpor until, sometime in the Neolithic period, he arrived in the Middle East and established a community on the shores of what was then the freshwater Black Sea.<br /> <br /> Many scholars believe the flood narrative is a remembrance (filtered through untold generations of oral history) of when the Black Sea flooded due to post Ice Age sea levels rising by more than a hundred meters c. 5500 BCE over the course of about a year.<br /> <br /> That would put the Second City in the late Neolithic with the collapse and subsequent diaspora possibly coinciding with the dawn of the Copper/Bronze Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T02:43:28-07:00","id":1387672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387448#post1387448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caine can be the first vampire without literally being the first murderer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Caine did the one thing no other human had done at that point. He committed willing murder. Before him, all battles were done in another reality between angels and most times weren't even fights or deadly. If one side was clearly the winner, the other side backed off.<br /> <br /> Caine murdering Abel is what caused his curse. The act of killing another human had never been heard of before him which is why God reacted with the initial curse form. The angels that met with him during his awakening reformed the curse to vampirism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T05:22:12-07:00","id":1387687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387617#post1387617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the prose it\u2019s unlikely it refers to the recent astronomical usage and is instead, as originally intended, an indeterminately long time; likely well over 100k years, probably slipping in and out of torpor until, sometime in the Neolithic period, he arrived in the Middle East and established a community on the shores of what was then the freshwater Black Sea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be around G\u00f6bekli Tepe, a temple dating back to the 10th\u20138th millennium BCE, in Turkey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T06:26:45-07:00","id":1387697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Riccardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387687#post1387687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could be around G\u00f6bekli Tepe, a temple dating back to the 10th\u20138th millennium BCE, in Turkey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be.<br /> <br /> More likely given the flood narrative is that it\u2019s 100m beneath the waves of the Black Sea. When the region flooded c. 5500 BCE, more than 100,000 km^2 were submerged (much like Sundaland and Dogerland were flooded as the Ice Age receded).<br /> <br /> For something really fun, due to the underwater topography, the deepest parts of the Black Sea are completely devoid of oxygen (and therefore life of any kind) and pitch black. What better place for one or more unknown Antediluvians believed killed in the Deluge to end up; sleeping in the blackness just waiting for Gehenna?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T07:22:21-07:00","id":1387709,"title":"","content":"I think it's more that Caine murdered Abel against the wishes of god. It's like killing someone's favourite puppy. Then Caine's all like &quot;God, this is your fault&quot; and God's mad. <br /> Could also be that most of the early bible stories are just alegories; it didn't literally take seven days to build the world, Adam and Eve weren't the only intelligent bipeds, just ones that caught God's attention and started creating culture and forming complicated opinions. <br /> <br /> <br /> In the begining there was a singular mass of soul, God separated from the mass and made the material world and then God <i>Imprisoned</i> the rest of the souls into the material world, the spirit world and triat formed from the material world, gaia grew to embody planet earth specifically, and as life grew they too created corrosponding spirits. After billions of years (and a few extinction events) humanity formed, a species God wanted to watch, as humans are both interesting and they have the potential to escape the material world's imprisonment, maybe neanderthals had this capability, but they died out and didn't write so... Anyhow, at some point the changing breeds come in. Also, God's been around for long stretches of time so his personality may shift. <br /> <br /> Here's a theory I just thought up while writing this<br /> Abel worked out agriculture, god was delighted as this would bring humanity closer to making cities. <br /> Caine killed Abel, either because he liked life as it was, or to spite the god that had trapped him. <br /> God curses Caine with Vampirism, a curse which was tailored to lead to the development of cities: needing swaths of humans to sustain itself while keeping the vampire fed, the vampire would embrace for company and create more need for city expansion, the quality of blood would decline each generation so that cities would have clear and strong hierarchies whilst also diablerie is a thing to prevent the vampires from getting complacant or moving out of the city to develop new cities (leaving for a new area with no vampires would deny any chance of promotion) and strife between vampires would lead to interesting developments. The banality vampires would come to put into urban life would infect the populace and prevent the Ascendance (escaping the materail prison) of humanity from the material prison they would otherwise escape. The strong blood would enable the vampires to survive their early nights, while it's weakening would force vampires to enter obscurity to avoid persecution within and without and thus keep the mortal populace as ignorant and uninspired &quot;sleepers&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T08:24:16-07:00","id":1387728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387709#post1387709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abel worked out agriculture, god was delighted as this would bring humanity closer to making cities. Caine killed Abel, either because he liked life as it was, or to spite the god that had trapped him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Abel was the shepherd and Cain the farmer. After Cain was banished according to tradition he became the forefather of the Canaanites.<br /> <br /> Historically, the Hebrews were shepherds in conflict with the agriculture-based Canaanites and so Cain and Abel can be taken as an allegory for these conflicts, particularly as justification for why the Hebrews were justified in driving the Canaanites out of the Holy Land.<br /> <br /> The funniest part for me if we\u2019re crossing the splats though is the notion that Caine isn\u2019t even a vampire. Lilith\u2019s botched effort to Awaken him caused Cain to go Marauder and create his own personal reality buffer where he\u2019s punishing himself eternally for all his sins... denied the community that fire provided, the light of the sun, able to sustain himself only on blood. This is why he could invent disciplines on the fly. Later he learned how to inflict a static version of his curse on others that was inserted into the consensus early enough that it\u2019s a permanent mythic thread which allows those suffering his curse to exist.<br /> <br /> But back on the topic at hand... I like the concept of generations because it does allow for \u201celder evils\u201d that only a group can hope to defeat; but also because of the one exception that sorta throws everything into question; Dhampirs are mechanically stronger than their 15th Gen parents. They can use all 10 self-regenerating blood points, can soak lethal damage with Stamina, are immune to sunlight and all aggravated damage (including fire) can be healed as if it were lethal. Sure, they\u2019re limited to one dot in disciplines, but there\u2019s a LOT you can do with those first dots and they don\u2019t have to pay double blood for any that use it either.<br /> <br /> Basically, nature went and came up with something stronger than all the blood sorcery of the ancients ever could (i.e. Revenants); likely due to the concept of hybrid vigor (basically the opposite of Revenant inbreeding).<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve sometimes toyed with the idea that the Last Daughter of Eve would be a Dhampir who becomes a New Eve to the hybrid generations which continue on after Gehenna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T08:42:04-07:00","id":1387731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387728#post1387728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funniest part for me if we\u2019re crossing the splats though is the notion that Caine isn\u2019t even a vampire. Lilith\u2019s botched effort to Awaken him caused Cain to go Marauder and create his own personal reality buffer where he\u2019s punishing himself eternally for all his sins... denied the community that fire provided, the light of the sun, able to sustain himself only on blood. This is why he could invent disciplines on the fly. Later he learned how to inflict a static version of his curse on others that was inserted into the consensus early enough that it\u2019s a permanent mythic thread which allows those suffering his curse to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are wankers who'd claim that wheels first spun because a mage made it so. <br /> <br /> <br /> But onto the Caine/Abel point. <br /> Alright, I got em mixed up. But even so, it's nice to go with what Becket said; Caine represents agrarian society whilst Abel represents a hunter-gatherer. Caine was trying to escape the eternal wanderings of the hunter gatherer and settle down; which would mean he'd be less occupied by procuring food and fending off predators and could instead build towards something, which could eventually mean civilisation and ascendance. Abel doing as people had always done, wandering the land for supplies, pleased God. So Caine killed abel and god went &quot;If you want cities, you can fucking have them&quot; and then cursed caine into being a vampire, a city parasite. Forever corrupting Caine's wish to bring humanity forward with agrarian civilisation. For as long as there are cities, there are vampires subverting them into shitholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T09:16:36-07:00","id":1387737,"title":"","content":"My interpretation is that YHVH (God) got pissed not because Abel was the first person ever murdered, but because Abel was the favorite of YHVH and because it was his own brother who murdered him.<br /> <br /> Also, for some reason Onyx Path added an \u201ce\u201d on the end of Cain\u2019s name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T09:17:31-07:00","id":1387739,"title":"","content":"The First Kinslaying, not necessarily The First Murder","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T10:00:09-07:00","id":1387748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387697#post1387697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For something really fun, due to the underwater topography, the deepest parts of the Black Sea are completely devoid of oxygen (and therefore life of any kind) and pitch black. What better place for one or more unknown Antediluvians believed killed in the Deluge to end up; sleeping in the blackness just waiting for Gehenna?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds great, love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T10:13:30-07:00","id":1387755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387737#post1387737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, for some reason Onyx Path added an \u201ce\u201d on the end of Cain\u2019s name.</div> </div> </div> </div>That happened long ago, back when White Wolf was writing and publishing everything in-house. I've heard a few different theories, ranging from &quot;that's how Ye Olde Englishe works, right? And the Bible is written in Ye Olde Englishe, right?&quot; to &quot;you can't trademark the name Cain unless you change something about it&quot;.<br /> <br /> In-universe, there's speculation in one of the clanbooks that some vampiric copyist wanted to make a text look older (and thus more valuable) by putting E's on the ends of words, and then it stuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T11:22:06-07:00","id":1387766,"title":"","content":"Getting a little bit back to the main topic, one thing that would be nice is if Generation was a little more of a trade off.<br /> <br /> We only really see it with the 15/16th Gen that they only take lethal damage from sunlight, can hold down food without a merit and occasional bouts of biological function. But I think it\u2019d be interesting if it were a little more gradated.<br /> <br /> For example, say Gens 7- gets those rank 6+ disciplines and other traits, but Gens 8-14 can soak sunlight with Stamina (its still aggravated so you really can\u2019t stand out in it, but incidental indirect sunlight because a curtain gets moved might only result in a stinging sensation and some hissing instead of needing 24 hours and 5 blood points).<br /> <br /> Maybe gens 10-14 can hold down drink (possibly soup) for an hour.<br /> <br /> Maybe there\u2019s a sliding difficulty scale on the Beast where those of 7- have +1 diff to resist Frenzy while those 10-13 are -1 difficulty and 14-16 are -2 difficulty.<br /> <br /> Basically you\u2019re lacking in vampiric power, but are ever so slightly more human with each step away from Caine you take until it culminates with Dhampirs as actual live births from those vampires whose curse is so weak they can\u2019t even pass it on through the Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 05-12-2020, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T11:42:11-07:00","id":1387768,"title":"","content":"I actually really don't like that V5 has quantified that being low gen has loads of downsides aside from being more attractive to diablerists. Methuselah's thirst was supposed to be a mystery, a terrifying rumor, not something you definitely get after a certain amount of blood potency. You're not supposed to be happy about being 12th gen because having strong blood is debilitating and eating your way up would do as much harm as good. Thinbloods aren't supposed to blade, they're not meant to be special alchemists with practices that stronger vampires can't obtain. Low gens are meant to be mysterious, thin bloods are meant to be unfortunate. Stronger blood is meant to be highly desirable, not a double edged sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T12:12:27-07:00","id":1387774,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24808_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24808\" data-vbnamecard=\"24808\">Draconis</a> hmm, interesting. And true. \u201cCain\u201d can\u2019t be trademarked; \u201cCaine\u201d can be. (I asked my friend who\u2019s a trademark lawyer.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T13:40:45-07:00","id":1387798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387774#post1387774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24808_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24808\" data-vbnamecard=\"24808\">Draconis</a> hmm, interesting. And true. \u201cCain\u201d can\u2019t be trademarked; \u201cCaine\u201d can be. (I asked my friend who\u2019s a trademark lawyer.)</div> </div> </div> </div>See also the vampire-focused &quot;Legacy of Kain&quot; series of video games.<br /> <br /> And the professional wrassler known as &quot;Kane,&quot; whose character was created specifically to serve the role of a dangerous antagonist to his fictional brother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T14:39:49-07:00","id":1387810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387768#post1387768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually really don't like that V5 has quantified that being low gen has loads of downsides aside from being more attractive to diablerists...</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't say! How positively shocking! I would have never surmised there was something about V5 you didn't like!<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, I think V5 took the right approach with the generation background but also overdid it. The problem is how generation combines with V5's morality system. The fact is lower generation vampires have higher blood potency and thus have to drink from humans to feed, which in the long run will cause stains and after a fashion almost inevitable degeneration. This means a newly embraced 5th generation vampire (they are unlikely but they MIGHT happen) is going to be powerful (more dices to roll compared to high gen neonates, more effective disciplines) but at the same time risks wassail pretty quickly. This I don't like because I believe degeneration should come as a consequence of a player's behaviour and not be caused by a stroke of bad luck with the dices.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T22:29:28-07:00","id":1387910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387810#post1387810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't say! How positively shocking! I would have never surmised there was something about V5 you didn't like!<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, I think V5 took the right approach with the generation background but also overdid it. The problem is how generation combines with V5's morality system. The fact is lower generation vampires have higher blood potency and thus have to drink from humans to feed, which in the long run will cause stains and after a fashion almost inevitable degeneration. This means a newly embraced 5th generation vampire (they are unlikely but they MIGHT happen) is going to be powerful (more dices to roll compared to high gen neonates, more effective disciplines) but at the same time risks wassail pretty quickly. This I don't like because I believe degeneration should come as a consequence of a player's behaviour and not be caused by a stroke of bad luck with the dices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. A 5th generation vampire embraced today can get 1 hunger per human, so they aren't going to be getting stains unless they have highly restrictive hunger. This hypothetical neonate while he will have to kill humans to get hunger below 2 after 100 years assuming he doesn't torpor, also starts out with the ability to re-roll rouse checks for level 2 and lower disciplines meaning that he can more safely rely upon more powerful disciplines to assist in feeding without risking hunger compared to even the average ancillae.<br /> <br /> Hell, even let's assume that this hypothetical 5th gen stays awake for five hundred years consecutively. He can't reduce hunger below 3 without killing but can reroll a rouse check for any discipline power. This means that he has about as much blood for his powers as he could possibly need. Yes, he will have to mildly hurt a human to get any blood from them, but even if he kills one human a day (And assuming each day is a session) that's a 50% chance to degenerate at humanity 8 or higher. 25% at 7, 15% at 6, 11% at 5. Which, it's relatively high except this is also a methuselah's child, they are going to be pretty disturbed AND it's avoidable with the right conviction to the point that they might be able to justify their daily murders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T01:03:20-07:00","id":1387949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387810#post1387810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't say! How positively shocking! I would have never surmised there was something about V5 you didn't like!<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, I think V5 took the right approach with the generation background but also overdid it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm entirely fair with V5. I acknowledge what's good, bad and ugly. I don't try to make it sound all bad just because I think the overall product is bad and completely undermines a perfect setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Previous editions hinted somewhat at what's possibly blood potency; Diablerie increased how pale you were (Or dark, in the case of Assamites; maybe it also increased how ugly you were, in the case of such clans) but that could be seen as stealing years, which had no mechanical effect. Similarly getting a &quot;I can only drink this kind of blood&quot; happened, but you could chalk that up to belief effecting the vampire (IE can't cross running water, afraid of garlic, can only drink the blood of virgins.)<br /> V5 also has a possession mechanic for diablerie, and although I don't like it (Humanity is really the worst thing for diablerie to roll; Is the game encouraging high humanity vampires to eat more and baring it for those on low humanity?) it is nice to have something written down so you aren't at the personal whims of your storyteller who could be a big moralizing softie and who might have you possessed for just consuming anyone at all. But after you diablerise you choose how to distribute your points? Eh. That's something that really takes the magic out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T04:20:08-07:00","id":1387976,"title":"","content":"I do not have V5 be because it is still going to be released in the DACHL region but from my opinion yes it is worth keeping the Generations. Because it gives two fundamental core elements of the game.<br /> 1. No matter how much time you are going to invest you will always be weaker as vampires with lower generation that have lived at least the same time as you until you are villing to consume souls.<br /> 2. It defines who created you in many ways. Not only he going to be your protege like in Roman Politic or in Feudalism but even what generation you are and so how others see you. If for example the rare case a vampire from an Elder or Methuselahm Generation decides to Embrace a fledgling many other vampires seek him as a chance for an upgrade for them and so his life get harder just because those people want his soul because he got (un)lucky to embraced by such an old and mighty vampire.<br /> <br /> The other reason I like the Generation System are the thinbloods. In the Dark Ages there where thinbloods too. It whas interpreted as a sign of Gehenna though those born with thin blood flaw would have a few centuries later on the same generation no such flaw regularly. Thin Bloods are a sign of that the boundaries of blood(curse) getting expanded and/or reaching its limit with low End of Dhampirs that only have one dot, can not be (anymore) Ghouled and have the ability to walk in Daylight for the cost of having no immortality. So you have to decide of how mighty as a Vampire and how much human you want to be. Those Daylightvampires that can be fine out there would have been in V20 Dhampirs or Generation 16 that can only go out with full cover and on cloudy days because latter still need to fear for getting ignited by the sun. And the Alchemy and having the strangest self made disciplines that whas already Time of the Thin Bloods.<br /> <br /> In our rounds before BJD there where only two generations if you did not play Pander or got other GM order for game. 7/8 for DA/MA or 15 because he can eat, accept more or less sunlight and most important get children without having to sacrifice immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T08:28:32-07:00","id":1388054,"title":"","content":"Dhampirs and immortality is a bit nebulous; while in-universe characters have associated them with Revenants, there are both physiological and mechanical differences between them.<br /> <br /> Revenants have extended childhoods due to aging slowly overall, Dhampirs age normally until their vampiric abilities kick in at which point their aging halts (and a point is made that it would suck if this happened in early puberty). Dhampirs are supposed to be young (under 20 at time ToTB came out) so whether this was just greatly retarded aging or its outright stopped is up in the air.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, Revenants spend blood just as ghouls do... burning it is a physical process (which is why V20 limited the volume/number of points they could hold) while for Dhampirs the \u201cblood points\u201d are entirely metaphysical... expending all of them doesn\u2019t change their blood volume at all (and V20 leaves them access to all 10 points as a result).<br /> <br /> The result is that, depending on the role you intend Dhampirs to play in your campaign, you could reasonably set their lifespans as anywhere from Revenant to actual immortal.<br /> <br /> Example 1: Gehenna is imminent, the Last Daughter of Eve is a Dhampir who will become a New Eve as both vampires and baseline humans go extinct. For this a finite lifespan (so that the new line of humans doesn\u2019t rapidly overwhelm the environment since they never die off) makes total sense.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Remember how the first humans in the Bible were said to live for hundreds of years, the lifespans slowly descending to normal human lifespans? \u201cAll of this has happened before and will happen again.\u201d [Insert \u201cAll Along the Watchtower\u201d riff here]<br /> <br /> Example 2: Gehenna is of the less severe cyclical variety and Dhampirs do not breed true (i.e. their children are just ordinary humans). Here you could go with the \u201cwho wants to live forever?\u201d trope with immortality as more a curse than a blessing (you\u2019ll forever look 13-18 years old, all your mortal friends will die, any children you have will die of old age, but you aren\u2019t welcome in the courts of the undead nor can you sleep away the ages so that when you wake everything can be fresh and new).<br /> <br /> In this case, it might be interesting to reveal the existing of elder Dhampirs. During the Dark Ages the 13th generation was thin-blooded. Perhaps those pathetic medieval thin-bloods produced Dhampirs that are now a thousand years old with the same long views as the Methuselahs, but without having been able to sleep away the ages so they\u2019ve become as depraved as the Revenants.<br /> <br /> Such fiends might actually make an interesting counterpoint to the low generation elders... that the weakest might overcome even the strongest by being able to marshal forces outside the elder\u2019s usual command... to not be driven to feed and to walk in daylight for a thousand years with even one dot in Dominate and Presence could give them command of mortal institutions well beyond a typical elder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:37:24-07:00","id":1388142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387810#post1387810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jokes aside, I think V5 took the right approach with the generation background but also overdid it. The problem is how generation combines with V5's morality system. The fact is lower generation vampires have higher blood potency and thus have to drink from humans to feed, which in the long run will cause stains and after a fashion almost inevitable degeneration. This means a newly embraced 5th generation vampire (they are unlikely but they MIGHT happen) is going to be powerful (more dices to roll compared to high gen neonates, more effective disciplines) but at the same time risks wassail pretty quickly. This I don't like because I believe degeneration should come as a consequence of a player's behaviour and not be caused by a stroke of bad luck with the dices.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I've done is separate Generation and Blood Potency. Generation determines the strength of Blood Surges and healing while increasing Bane Severity, While Blood Potency, squashed into a 5 point scale, determines your ability to reroll Discipline Rouse Checks and your feeding restrictions. Generation is static without diablerie, BP increases with age but in a nonlinear fashion (BP0-&gt;1 takes about a year, BP2 fifty years, BP3 a hundred, BP4 two hundred, BP5 four hundred).<br /> <br /> I find Generation too useful to throw out, but really don't like V5's 'generation dependent maximum and minimum BP' to be clunky and not what I want, so I ended up splitting the job of BP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T14:25:06-07:00","id":1388155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1388054#post1388054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dhampirs and immortality is a bit nebulous; while in-universe characters have associated them with Revenants, there are both physiological and mechanical differences between them.<br /> <br /> Revenants have extended childhoods due to aging slowly overall, Dhampirs age normally until their vampiric abilities kick in at which point their aging halts (and a point is made that it would suck if this happened in early puberty). Dhampirs are supposed to be young (under 20 at time ToTB came out) so whether this was just greatly retarded aging or its outright stopped is up in the air.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, Revenants spend blood just as ghouls do... burning it is a physical process (which is why V20 limited the volume/number of points they could hold) while for Dhampirs the \u201cblood points\u201d are entirely metaphysical... expending all of them doesn\u2019t change their blood volume at all (and V20 leaves them access to all 10 points as a result).<br /> <br /> The result is that, depending on the role you intend Dhampirs to play in your campaign, you could reasonably set their lifespans as anywhere from Revenant to actual immortal.<br /> <br /> Example 1: Gehenna is imminent, the Last Daughter of Eve is a Dhampir who will become a New Eve as both vampires and baseline humans go extinct. For this a finite lifespan (so that the new line of humans doesn\u2019t rapidly overwhelm the environment since they never die off) makes total sense.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Remember how the first humans in the Bible were said to live for hundreds of years, the lifespans slowly descending to normal human lifespans? \u201cAll of this has happened before and will happen again.\u201d [Insert \u201cAll Along the Watchtower\u201d riff here]<br /> <br /> Example 2: Gehenna is of the less severe cyclical variety and Dhampirs do not breed true (i.e. their children are just ordinary humans). Here you could go with the \u201cwho wants to live forever?\u201d trope with immortality as more a curse than a blessing (you\u2019ll forever look 13-18 years old, all your mortal friends will die, any children you have will die of old age, but you aren\u2019t welcome in the courts of the undead nor can you sleep away the ages so that when you wake everything can be fresh and new).<br /> <br /> In this case, it might be interesting to reveal the existing of elder Dhampirs. During the Dark Ages the 13th generation was thin-blooded. Perhaps those pathetic medieval thin-bloods produced Dhampirs that are now a thousand years old with the same long views as the Methuselahs, but without having been able to sleep away the ages so they\u2019ve become as depraved as the Revenants.<br /> <br /> Such fiends might actually make an interesting counterpoint to the low generation elders... that the weakest might overcome even the strongest by being able to marshal forces outside the elder\u2019s usual command... to not be driven to feed and to walk in daylight for a thousand years with even one dot in Dominate and Presence could give them command of mortal institutions well beyond a typical elder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misread our missremember something because in BJD on 144 it is clearly said, that aging get slowed down but never stops. About Dhampirs do not breed true, this is stated there too, that they can get mortal children. About cycnical Gehenna until you are houserule it this is not technically possible because it is clearly said, Dhampirs can only be born from 15+ vampires.<br /> Though because there are earlier sources about Dhampires in history I am going to think their whas another way for dhampires to be born. Mayby Golconda made such a wonder possible?<br /> But yeah it is not said how slow Dhampirs age so technically you could say one human year is for Dhampire one hundred years or something like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T10:28:44-07:00","id":1388353,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> I love your cosmology! (Sorry. I find cosmology fascinating. Almost as fascinating as romantic and emotional stuff.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T14:15:34-07:00","id":1388430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1388353#post1388353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> I love your cosmology! (Sorry. I find cosmology fascinating. Almost as fascinating as romantic and emotional stuff.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Although to be fair I took heavy inspiration from DtF, WtO, MtA and of course VtM in order to make things work. I find DtF in particular is good for bridging all other cosmologies.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T14:35:56-07:00","id":1388435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1387949#post1387949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm entirely fair with V5. I acknowledge what's good, bad and ugly. I don't try to make it sound all bad just because I think the overall product is bad and completely undermines a perfect setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you believe that. To me and to many others you just seem like someone who really hates V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Previous editions hinted somewhat at what's possibly blood potency; Diablerie increased how pale you were (Or dark, in the case of Assamites; maybe it also increased how ugly you were, in the case of such clans) but that could be seen as stealing years, which had no mechanical effect. Similarly getting a &quot;I can only drink this kind of blood&quot; happened, but you could chalk that up to belief effecting the vampire (IE can't cross running water, afraid of garlic, can only drink the blood of virgins.)<br /> V5 also has a possession mechanic for diablerie, and although I don't like it (Humanity is really the worst thing for diablerie to roll; Is the game encouraging high humanity vampires to eat more and baring it for those on low humanity?) it is nice to have something written down so you aren't at the personal whims of your storyteller who could be a big moralizing softie and who might have you possessed for just consuming anyone at all. But after you diablerise you choose how to distribute your points? Eh. That's something that really takes the magic out of it. </div> </div> </div>I pretty much disagree with all of what you wrote here. Diablerie is not supposed to be a &quot;normal way&quot; to increase one's power. It's a damning act meant to emphasize that power comes at a terrible cost and one ha sto be willing to compromise his morality in order to get it. The ST who stresses these aspects is far from being a &quot; big moralizing softie&quot;, it's just someone who isn't willing to let players eat soulsfor kicks doing so scot free.<br /> I also find the idea that you need &quot;hard rules&quot; to keep the ST in check to be juvenile at best. The ST is working with the players to tell a story, not against them and the ST system was always meant to give space to the narration rather than representing a simulation with many specific rules.<br /> Lastly, calling VtM the &quot;perfect setting&quot; is an exageration. The setting has changed several times and is extremely inconsistent as different authors kept contraddicting each other even on the smallest of details like dates, ages and the like. Like it or not at the moment V5 presents a vision for VtM that's more coherent than what we had 15 years ago (there are still questionable choices though, like Theo Bell killing Hardestadt and being conisdered a fair mediator by the Camarilla...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T16:53:20-07:00","id":1388489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1388435#post1388435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (there are still questionable choices though, like Theo Bell killing Hardestadt and being conisdered a fair mediator by the Camarilla...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Does anyone run a game where the Ventrue powers that be didn't have Bell assassinated for killing such a powerful symbol of the clan? Bell isn't strong enough to survive on the run let alone trying to stay in the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T00:11:29-07:00","id":1388589,"title":"","content":"What's more horrifying, for you to eat souls and having to battle for your sanity as their soul clashes with yours, or for you to eat souls, feel absolutely orgasmic about the experience, and suffer no serious consequences other than possible persecution by the law?<br /> <br /> What's scarier; for a heinous crime to be unrewarding and damaging, or for a heinous crime to be<i> easy</i>? For me, it's definetly the latter. I'm not saying it should be normalized; I will have you killed if you do it at my table and get caught. I won't bullshit that some elders are ok with it to help you save your character. I'll kill your character if you're stupid enough to not make your escape. But from a perspective of 'it's god's curse' it's a whole lot more terrifying to Diablerie having no physical/mental consequences besides the perpetrator wanting to do more, having a creepy effect on mortals for a month and having a mark in their aura for a year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T01:45:25-07:00","id":1388602,"title":"","content":"I think that's really one of those situations where it depends on one personal tastes and what sort of theme or mood your trying to invoke in the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T02:15:29-07:00","id":1388611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1388489#post1388489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does anyone run a game where the Ventrue powers that be didn't have Bell assassinated for killing such a powerful symbol of the clan? Bell isn't strong enough to survive on the run let alone trying to stay in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do. In my games, having Theo Bell as an mediator kinda makes sense. For me at least. He did unite a lot of Anarchs behind his actions and has gained quite the following, reputation and say in Anarch matters. If you get him to agree to something, it's one of your best bets to have a lot of licks follow his advice/example, than to convince dozens of coteries with wildly different interests and long term goals of the same thing. Of course, not everyone agrees with keeping him around. Some of those are gunning for his head. But not the smartest ones, and not the mightiest ones. If someone gets too close to take him of the board, having that hound reassigned just made an item on the list, something to bargain for with Mr. Bell, to get him to do what you want. For everyone involved a dangerous (albeit interesting) game indeed.<br /> <br /> To say something on topic: Yes, Generations are really worthwhile in V:tM. At least to my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","name":"Pangur B\u00e1n","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T07:17:29-07:00","id":1388671,"title":"","content":"Not killing Bell is an open invitation to kill members of the Inner Circle even taking the Ventrue out of it. Some crimes are just too big to be forgiven or over looked. In my world anyway, I'm not saying anyone has to play like me, just saying it would be like everyone knowing who killed the President (US) and basically where he was and not only taking him out but instead using him in a diplomatic role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T08:16:06-07:00","id":1388684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1388489#post1388489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does anyone run a game where the Ventrue powers that be didn't have Bell assassinated for killing such a powerful symbol of the clan? Bell isn't strong enough to survive on the run let alone trying to stay in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not running anything atm but if I were I would have Theo Bell be alive, working for the anarchs and opposing the Camarilla who would be trying to get rid of him having declared Theo anathema.<br /> <br /> As for Theo Bell not being strong enough to surrvive... he was literally the last vampire left standing during Gehenna and he has managed to kill/incapacitate the likes of Vitel, Karsh, the 2 diabolist masters of Karsh and Hardestadt... Theo Bell is one tough and mean sob...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T14:30:41-07:00","id":1389072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387325-are-generations-really-worthwhile-in-vtm?p=1388684#post1388684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Theo Bell not being strong enough to surrvive... he was literally the last vampire left standing during Gehenna and he has managed to kill/incapacitate the likes of Vitel, Karsh, the 2 diabolist masters of Karsh and Hardestadt... Theo Bell is one tough and mean sob...</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is insane, to any reasonable person, he doesn't have the stat block to take on Karsh or Hardestadt. Probably explains why I considered the Novels non-canon unless the info also appeared in an actual Tabletop book. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}